# Single source of truth for the verify-gate example list.
# Both tools/verify.sh and tools/verify.ps1 read from this file.
#
# Format: one example name per line (no .nr extension, no path prefix).
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Order matters — the gate runs them top-to-bottom.
#
# To add a new example:
#   1. Drop the .nr file in examples/<NN>_<name>.nr.
#   2. Add a line below.
#   3. Add a row to examples/README.md under the matching tier.
#   4. Re-run verify.sh / verify.ps1 to confirm it builds + runs.
#
# Special case: 07_rust_interop is added programmatically by the
# verify scripts only when stdlib/rods/rust_bridge/ has been built
# (libnucleor_rust_bridge.a / nucleor_rust_bridge.lib present).
# Do NOT list 07 here.
#
# Showcases (examples/showcase/*.nr — lorenz, vqe_h2, market_maker,
# wing_simulator, robotic_arm) are intentionally NOT in this list.
# They are exercised separately by the showcase-build step in
# verify.sh / verify.ps1 (search for "showcase" / "vqe_h2" in the
# script). Showcases are discovery-grade demos rather than gated
# language invariants, so they live under their own step rather
# than the per-example loop fed by this file.

# Tier 1 — language tour
01_hello
02_fib
03_structs
04_rods
05_quantum
06_perf_attrs

